; Region-to-area's walk keeps the region it walks for across the interrupts
; it can take (sys/ucadr/uc-page-fault.lisp, REGION-TO-AREA-WALK).  Load
; lisp/region-area-map-interrupt.lisp first, interpreted or compiled; it needs
; revision 14 or 15.  Microcode that keeps the region in A-TEM1 puts an area
; into region 0's byte when the tick comes during the walk: the storms below
; (timer 0 at 200 and 50 microseconds) find region 0's byte holding another
; area's number.
;
; Preconditions: the table found in A memory, and the tick tracking the
; mouse.
(rgm-find-map) => (T)
(rgm-mouse-tracking) => T
; The controls: the table as the system left it, and a storm at the tick's
; own period.
(rgm-bad) => NIL
(rgm-storm 16667) => NIL
; The storms.
(rgm-storm 200) => NIL
(rgm-storm 50) => NIL
(rgm-storm 50) => NIL
